From 263e8d1e659f2fb06ad64f737979917cfe505a45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Jeffrey R. Day" <phroun@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 11:25:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Catch the wiki up to v0.1.31

The four directional alignment words are natural and opposite now, which
says what they are opposite TO; a tree column's align takes the same seven
words and its widths are units, eight to a character cell; a treeview's
rows and columns are items= and columns=; and fixed_left/fixed_right count
along the run as fixed_begin/fixed_end.

The list of what direction does not yet reach was written before the
chrome followed it, and named six things of which four now turn over.
Tab order and a dock row's entries are what is left.
