-## Where "begin" is
+## Where "natural" is
 
 Four of the seven horizontal values are **logical**: they name a side by which
 way text runs there, and swap over in a right-to-left context. Two are
 **optical**: they name a physical side and nothing moves them.
 
+NATURAL is the side a direction reads from — where something goes when nothing
+fights the reading. OPPOSITE is the other side of the same box, and what it is
+opposite TO is the natural side named in the same word: the trinket's own text
+for the text pair, the surrounding layout's for the layout pair.
+
 | `halign` | Left-to-right | Right-to-left | Stated against |
 |---|---|---|---|
-| `textbegin` | left | right | the trinket's **own text** |
-| `textend` | right | left | the trinket's **own text** |
-| `layoutbegin` | left | right | the **container** it sits in |
-| `layoutend` | right | left | the **container** it sits in |
+| `textnatural` | left | right | the trinket's **own text** |
+| `textopposite` | right | left | the trinket's **own text** |
+| `layoutnatural` | left | right | the **container** it sits in |
+| `layoutopposite` | right | left | the **container** it sits in |
 | `center` | centre | centre | nothing |
 | `opticalleft` | left | left | nothing |
 | `opticalright` | right | right | nothing |
 
 The two pairs differ only where the two directions disagree — an English caption
-in a right-to-left form. `textbegin` keeps that caption's left edge; `layoutbegin`
-puts it on the right with everything else in the form.
+in a right-to-left form. `textnatural` keeps that caption's left edge;
+`layoutnatural` puts it on the right with everything else in the form.
 
 `valign` has no logical values. Rows run top to bottom in every direction.
 
